WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.892
NOT EXISTS expresses the anti-match directly.

00:00:03.892 --> 00:00:11.082
For each patient, the inner query searches for a review-queue row with the same patient ID.

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:13.932
If no matching row exists, the patient is kept.

00:00:13.932 --> 00:00:22.417
The unrelated NULL row does not create the same problem because it does not match the current patient ID.

00:00:22.417 --> 00:00:28.327
This is why NOT EXISTS is often the clearer starting point for anti-join questions.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:33.387
EXISTS asks whether at least one related row satisfies the condition.

00:00:33.387 --> 00:00:37.302
The selected columns inside EXISTS usually do not matter; the existence of a row does.

00:00:37.302 --> 00:00:45.712
This maps naturally to questions such as patients with any follow-up, customers with any purchase,

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.600
or orders with no shipment record.
